1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,154
Every place in your universe so far

2
00:00:02,604 --> 00:00:05,512
is somewhere the crew looks at from the bridge.

3
00:00:07,312 --> 00:00:08,647
This one they fly into.

4
00:00:09,547 --> 00:00:11,671
And then one of them gets out.

5
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:14,897
By the end of this lecture

6
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:17,098
your universe has a ruin in it,

7
00:00:17,548 --> 00:00:19,546
and a story that runs through its rooms.

8
00:00:20,746 --> 00:00:23,522
Writing a ruin is a whole class of its own.

9
00:00:24,422 --> 00:00:27,658
So today I'm handing you one, finished.

10
00:00:29,458 --> 00:00:31,729
What we're learning is how a universe holds it.

11
00:00:32,629 --> 00:00:35,436
A ruin in a universe never says where it is.

12
00:00:35,886 --> 00:00:37,233
The landmark says that.

13
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:41,609
It needs one place marked as its entrance.

14
00:00:42,509 --> 00:00:44,302
And it needs two keys.

15
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:47,872
One on the thing that blocks the way,

16
00:00:48,322 --> 00:00:50,347
and one on the ruin itself.

17
00:00:51,547 --> 00:00:53,775
A new file, called hollow.

18
00:00:54,675 --> 00:00:56,189
I paste the whole ruin in.

19
00:00:57,989 --> 00:01:00,462
Don't read every line, just read its shape.

20
00:01:02,262 --> 00:01:04,516
Three rooms, joined by passages,

21
00:01:04,966 --> 00:01:06,138
and one way in.

22
00:01:07,038 --> 00:01:09,437
A slab, fallen across one doorway.

23
00:01:10,337 --> 00:01:13,512
And behind the slab, a niche with a stone bowl in it.

24
00:01:15,312 --> 00:01:16,560
The bowl is an item,

25
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:20,069
and it lives in this file with the ruin.

26
00:01:21,269 --> 00:01:23,523
Now the landmark, in the universe file.

27
00:01:24,423 --> 00:01:26,342
It's a landmark like any other,

28
00:01:26,792 --> 00:01:28,340
with two more lines.

29
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:31,998
Relic, and the ruin's key.

30
00:01:32,898 --> 00:01:34,920
Relic file, and the name of the file.

31
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:37,871
That's the whole join.

32
00:01:38,771 --> 00:01:40,197
And there's no terrain line,

33
00:01:40,647 --> 00:01:43,364
because a ruin brings its own cloud.

34
00:01:44,564 --> 00:01:45,801
And now the story.

35
00:01:46,701 --> 00:01:48,786
A lead that takes the crew there.

36
00:01:49,686 --> 00:01:51,879
A step that's done when the slab is cut.

37
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:55,008
And a step that's done when the bowl is taken.

38
00:01:56,808 --> 00:01:58,111
Look at those two signals.

39
00:01:59,011 --> 00:02:00,248
I didn't make them up,

40
00:02:00,698 --> 00:02:02,562
and nothing in my files sends them,

41
00:02:03,012 --> 00:02:04,710
because the game does.

42
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:09,559
It builds each word from a key in the ruin's file.

43
00:02:10,459 --> 00:02:13,445
Slab, then opened, and hollow, then taken.

44
00:02:15,245 --> 00:02:18,771
And each briefing is a page, as in Lecture Seven.

45
00:02:19,671 --> 00:02:21,515
The cut gets two icon bullets,

46
00:02:21,965 --> 00:02:23,958
who suits up, and what they cut.

47
00:02:25,158 --> 00:02:27,846
I run lint, and all seven files are clean.

48
00:02:29,646 --> 00:02:31,510
Lint looked in the ruin's file.

49
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:34,327
It found a barrier called slab,

50
00:02:34,777 --> 00:02:38,286
so it knows the game sends slab opened.

51
00:02:40,086 --> 00:02:41,984
Watch what happens if I get the word wrong.

52
00:02:42,884 --> 00:02:45,382
There's one warning, on the step that waits,

53
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:48,414
and it says nothing sends that word.

54
00:02:49,314 --> 00:02:51,404
So I fix it, and it's clean again.

55
00:02:52,604 --> 00:02:53,476
Let's go in, then.

56
00:02:54,376 --> 00:02:56,295
There's a fourth lead in the quest log,

57
00:02:56,745 --> 00:02:58,007
and I engage it.

58
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:00,012
The Hollow is charted,

59
00:03:00,462 --> 00:03:02,018
and the next step appears.

60
00:03:03,818 --> 00:03:06,009
I bring the ship up to the way in.

61
00:03:06,909 --> 00:03:09,951
And now a handheld has something new on it.

62
00:03:10,401 --> 00:03:11,854
It says suit up.

63
00:03:12,754 --> 00:03:13,851
So out I go.

64
00:03:14,751 --> 00:03:16,770
The suit knows two places,

65
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,167
the gallery door and the niche.

66
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:23,410
At the door, the slab is a target.

67
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:26,693
I cut it, and that takes twelve seconds.

68
00:03:27,592 --> 00:03:29,384
The step is done, and paid.

69
00:03:30,284 --> 00:03:31,819
Then on to the niche.

70
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:33,986
The bowl comes with me,

71
00:03:34,436 --> 00:03:35,754
and that's the last step.

72
00:03:36,954 --> 00:03:39,310
I have to be honest about what you just saw.

73
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:43,083
When I checked this page, a script flew all of it,

74
00:03:43,533 --> 00:03:45,490
and nobody was watching a screen.

75
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:52,041
And the exosuit had one known fault, in older versions of the game.

76
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,046
A console could close the first time it met one mid-game.

77
00:03:56,946 --> 00:03:58,071
It's fixed now,

78
00:03:58,521 --> 00:04:03,022
and if your game is older, the way round it is on the page.

79
00:04:04,222 --> 00:04:07,456
Now the part that makes a ruin fit a campaign.

80
00:04:09,256 --> 00:04:11,226
I go home, and I come back.

81
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:13,973
The game rebuilt the whole place.

82
00:04:14,423 --> 00:04:15,994
And the slab's still cut.

83
00:04:16,894 --> 00:04:18,099
The bowl's still gone,

84
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:20,197
and nobody paid me twice.

85
00:04:21,997 --> 00:04:24,687
Now I close the game, and continue,

86
00:04:25,137 --> 00:04:26,342
and it's the same again.

87
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,914
And here it is in the save.

88
00:04:30,364 --> 00:04:33,297
The ruin, what was opened, and what was taken.

89
00:04:34,497 --> 00:04:36,156
One note before you go on.

90
00:04:37,056 --> 00:04:40,319
The battle lectures were written for a universe with no ruin.

91
00:04:41,219 --> 00:04:43,755
So three small things read differently there,

92
00:04:44,205 --> 00:04:45,738
and they're listed on the page.

93
00:04:47,538 --> 00:04:48,540
Now it's your turn.

94
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:52,204
Give The Hollow your own name and your own words.

95
00:04:53,104 --> 00:04:54,141
Play it to the bowl.

96
00:04:54,591 --> 00:04:57,292
Go home, come back, and look at that slab.
